{"engine_version":"0.29.3","file":"leo-ppp-convergence.toml","toml":"# Precise point positioning (PPP) convergence with LEO augmentation.\n#\n# A float PPP filter on ionosphere-free code and phase runs at three mid-latitude sites with\n# GPS, Galileo, BeiDou (medium Earth orbit) and GLONASS, and then with each of four LEO\n# constellations added. Li et al. (\"LEO constellation-augmented multi-GNSS for rapid PPP\n# convergence\", Journal of Geodesy 93:749-764, 2019, doi 10.1007/s00190-018-1195-2) report\n# multi-GNSS convergence shortened from 9.6 min to 7.0, 3.2, 2.1 and 1.3 min with 60, 96, 192\n# and 288 LEO satellites; `compare_li_2019` puts those figures beside the modelled ones.\n#\n# The four LEO constellations here are representative Walker delta shells at 1000 km and\n# 60 deg with 60, 96, 192 and 288 satellites; they are NOT the paper's designs, and the noise,\n# stations and convergence definition (horizontal and vertical errors below 10 cm until the\n# end of the run) are this model's. The comparison is therefore a MODELLED consistency check\n# on the trend: convergence must shorten monotonically with the number of LEO satellites.\nkind = \"leo-ppp\"\nseed = 20\nduration_s = 1800.0\nstep_s = 10.0\nruns = 4\ncompare_li_2019 = true\n\n[[site]]\nlat_deg = 30.5\nlon_deg = 114.4\n\n[[site]]\nlat_deg = 48.1\nlon_deg = 11.6\n\n[[site]]\nlat_deg = 39.0\nlon_deg = -77.0\n\n[[gnss]]\nname = \"GPS\"\npreset = \"gps-baseline\"\nmask_deg = 7.0\n\n[[gnss]]\nname = \"Galileo\"\npreset = \"galileo\"\nmask_deg = 7.0\n\n[[gnss]]\nname = \"BeiDou\"\npreset = \"beidou-meo\"\nmask_deg = 7.0\n\n[[gnss]]\nname = \"GLONASS\"\npreset = \"glonass\"\nmask_deg = 7.0\n\n[[case]]\nname = \"60 LEO\"\n[[case.system]]\nname = \"LEO-60\"\nmask_deg = 7.0\n[[case.system.shell]]\ntotal = 60\nplanes = 6\nphasing = 1\naltitude_km = 1000.0\ninclination_deg = 60.0\n\n[[case]]\nname = \"96 LEO\"\n[[case.system]]\nname = \"LEO-96\"\nmask_deg = 7.0\n[[case.system.shell]]\ntotal = 96\nplanes = 8\nphasing = 1\naltitude_km = 1000.0\ninclination_deg = 60.0\n\n[[case]]\nname = \"192 LEO\"\n[[case.system]]\nname = \"LEO-192\"\nmask_deg = 7.0\n[[case.system.shell]]\ntotal = 192\nplanes = 12\nphasing = 1\naltitude_km = 1000.0\ninclination_deg = 60.0\n\n[[case]]\nname = \"288 LEO\"\n[[case.system]]\nname = \"LEO-288\"\nmask_deg = 7.0\n[[case.system.shell]]\ntotal = 288\nplanes = 16\nphasing = 1\naltitude_km = 1000.0\ninclination_deg = 60.0\n","summary":"PPP convergence to 0.10 m horizontal / 0.10 m vertical, 12 runs per case, 96 GNSS satellites\n  GNSS only                       0 LEO  median 7.4 min  converged 100%  NEES mean 3.13\n  60 LEO                         60 LEO  median 4.8 min  converged 100%  NEES mean 3.08\n  96 LEO                         96 LEO  median 3.2 min  converged 100%  NEES mean 2.74\n  192 LEO                       192 LEO  median 2.7 min  converged 100%  NEES mean 2.65\n  288 LEO                       288 LEO  median 2.3 min  converged 100%  NEES mean 3.06\n  Li et al. 2019 (published, min) vs modelled: 0:9.6/7.4 60:7.0/4.8 96:3.2/3.2 192:2.1/2.7 288:1.3/2.3\n","json":"{\n  \"cases\": [\n    {\n      \"convergence_min\": [\n        7.666666666666667,\n        8.5,\n        15.666666666666666,\n        7.0,\n        15.666666666666666,\n        7.166666666666667,\n        6.333333333333333,\n        3.6666666666666665,\n        6.666666666666667,\n        8.666666666666666,\n        8.166666666666666,\n        7.0\n      ],\n      \"fraction_converged\": 1.0,\n      \"mean_sats\": 29.171270718232044,\n      \"median_convergence_min\": 7.416666666666667,\n      \"median_horizontal_error_m\": [\n        0.45790363855639266,\n        0.22082336406161202,\n        0.12478783065174084,\n        0.10545215090606969,\n        0.10767601531425681,\n        0.09173925896818723,\n        0.07832262925264473,\n        0.08669300034477433,\n        0.07731431008522903,\n        0.06878163888340583,\n        0.06058179107911591,\n        0.04187257990395815